  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 8.2. Increased capacity of Member States to improve governance and sustainability of social protection systems</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To strengthen the delivery of social security, the SSF formalized a revised Communications and Outreach Strategy in 2022. The strategy proposes communication and outreach methods to improve communication and visibility of the various schemes under the SSF and improve and expand registration of employers and employees. Based on the strategy, the SSF developed communications content that ranges from videos and public service announcements aimed to educate the public on the schemes and based on the communications and outreach methos proposed by the Strategy. 
2) The SSF completed its first actuarial valuation in May 2023 aiming at drawing evidence to ensure the Fund&apos;s sustainability. It has thus implemented the legal requirement to ensure the monitoring of the financial sustainability of the social security scheme system and the policy measures to adopt to ensure its long-term financial sustainability. The valuation is also intended to further policy dialogue around the continuous development of the SSF&apos;s schemes and governance. 
. 1) With support from the EU and FCDO, the ILO supported the SSF in the drafting of the communications and outreach strategy. Specifically, the ILO provided technical assistance to conduct stakeholder mapping and identification of communication objectives for each targeted audience at the national and local levels through a participatory meeting with the SSF team and series of consultations with potential stakeholders. The outcomes from the participatory meetings and consultations were the main inputs in developing the communications and outreach strategy. 
2) With support from the EU, the ILO supported the SSF in conducting its first actuarial valuation and provided the necessary technical expertise. ILO also conducted actuarial valuation training for the SSF team to build actuarial and statistical, as well as administrative and operational capacity for future actuarial valuations and social security reforms.</narrative>
   </description>
